# ControlRig Solver Unit Allowlist Research

This note is the Phase 5 docs-only authority record for adding pose-changing
solver capability later. It does not approve implementation by itself.

## Scope

Current status: research only.

Do not add a solver unit allowlist entry, recipe schema, C++ route, Python route,
or asset fixture from this note alone. The implementation gate below must pass
first.

Stable authoring constraints remain unchanged:

- no original asset mutation;
- no writes outside `/Game/_MCP_Temp` or `/Game/_MCP_Sample`;
- no runtime/gameplay module;
- no arbitrary script struct names from user input;
- no generic Python reflection into protected ControlRig/RigVM internals;
- no serialized MCP-only references;
- no static C++ dependency from `UnrealMCP` to
  `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`.

## First Candidate Family

Recommended first implementation candidate:

| Purpose | Candidate |
| --- | --- |
| Simple pose-changing proof | `FRigUnit_SetTransform` |
| Header | `Engine/Plugins/Animation/ControlRig/Source/ControlRig/Public/Units/Hierarchy/RigUnit_SetTransform.h` |
| Runtime behavior | `Engine/Plugins/Animation/ControlRig/Source/ControlRig/Private/Units/Hierarchy/RigUnit_SetTransform.cpp` |
| Editor precedent | `ControlRigEditor.cpp` adds `FRigUnit_SetTransform::StaticStruct()` for the Set Transform shortcut |

Why this candidate:

- It is not deprecated in UE 5.6.1.
- It handles Bone, Control, Null, and other hierarchy element keys through
  `FRigElementKey`.
- It can prove FK-style propagation with one parent bone/control transform and
  `bPropagateToChildren=true`.
- Deprecated wrappers such as `FRigUnit_SetBoneTransform` and
  `FRigUnit_SetControlTransform` upgrade into `FRigUnit_SetTransform`, so they
  should not be first-class allowlist entries.

## Candidate Unit Contract

`FRigUnit_SetTransform` fields from the UE 5.6.1 header:

| Pin/field | Direction | Default observed in constructor | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `ExecuteContext` | mutable execute context | inherited | Link from an event unit before solve. |
| `Item` | input | `FRigElementKey(NAME_None, ERigElementType::Bone)` | Must be generated from reviewed recipe data, not free-form user struct text. |
| `Space` | input | `ERigVMTransformSpace::GlobalSpace` | Limit first pass to `GlobalSpace`; `LocalSpace` can follow after proof. |
| `bInitial` | input | `false` | Keep `false` in first pass; initial transforms have special Prepare/Begin behavior. |
| `Value` | input | identity `FTransform` | Structured recipe transform should serialize to this pin. |
| `Weight` | input | `1.0` | Clamp/validate to `0.0..1.0`; first fixture should use `1.0`. |
| `bPropagateToChildren` | input | `true` | Required for FK propagation proof. |
| `CachedIndex` | internal | empty cache | Must not be exposed in recipe input. |

Relevant supporting types:

- `ERigElementType` lives in `RigHierarchyDefines.h` and includes `Bone`,
  `Null`, `Control`, `Curve`, `Reference`, `Connector`, and `Socket`.
- `FRigElementKey` has `Type` and `Name`, plus a string constructor that parses
  `Type(Name)`.
- `ERigVMTransformSpace` lives in `RigVMFunctionDefines.h` and includes
  `LocalSpace` and `GlobalSpace`.

## Deferred Candidates

Do not use these as first implementation targets:

| Candidate | Reason |
| --- | --- |
| `FRigUnit_SetBoneTransform` | UE 5.6.1 marks it deprecated since 4.25 and upgrades it to `FRigUnit_SetTransform`. |
| `FRigUnit_SetControlTransform` | UE 5.6.1 marks it deprecated since 4.25 and upgrades it to `FRigUnit_SetTransform`. |
| `FRigUnit_SetTransformArray` | Deprecated since 5.0; use single unit proof first. |
| `FRigUnit_SetTransformItemArray` | Broader array schema and validation surface; defer until single transform proof is stable. |
| `FRigUnit_ParentConstraint` | Higher-level constraint unit with array/source settings; research separately after simple transform proof. |
| IK/Aim/Spine units | Need separate source-target-space, pole/up-vector, chain, and direct solve proof notes. |

## Proposed First Implementation Shape

Future recipe extension, not implemented yet:

```json
{
  "rigvm": {
    "units": [
      {
        "struct_name": "FRigUnit_SetTransform",
        "node_name": "PiperStable_SetPelvisTransform",
        "position": {"x": 260.0, "y": 0.0}
      }
    ],
    "pin_defaults": [
      {
        "pin_path": "PiperStable_SetPelvisTransform.Item",
        "default_value": "Bone(pelvis)"
      },
      {
        "pin_path": "PiperStable_SetPelvisTransform.Space",
        "default_value": "GlobalSpace"
      },
      {
        "pin_path": "PiperStable_SetPelvisTransform.bInitial",
        "default_value": "False"
      },
      {
        "pin_path": "PiperStable_SetPelvisTransform.Weight",
        "default_value": "1.0"
      },
      {
        "pin_path": "PiperStable_SetPelvisTransform.bPropagateToChildren",
        "default_value": "True"
      }
    ],
    "links": [
      {
        "source_pin_path": "PiperStable_BeginExecution.ExecuteContext",
        "target_pin_path": "PiperStable_SetPelvisTransform.ExecuteContext"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

The example default strings above are candidates only. Before implementation,
run `validate_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults` on a sample/temp target that
contains the unit and promote only validator-approved strings into a golden
fixture.

## Required Implementation Gate

Implementation can start only after a reviewed task explicitly approves solver unit expansion.
The first implementation should:

1. Add `FRigUnit_SetTransform` to the C++ allowlist only.
2. Include the exact UE 5.6.1 header for `FRigUnit_SetTransform`.
3. Add a narrow recipe schema for one or more reviewed set-transform specs.
4. Validate item type/name against authored or imported hierarchy readback.
5. Validate `Space` to `GlobalSpace` only for the first pass.
6. Force `bInitial=false` for the first pass.
7. Clamp `Weight` to `0.0..1.0`.
8. Keep `bPropagateToChildren` explicit in the recipe and report.
9. Validate all pin defaults through the existing recipe validation path.
10. Link only reviewed execute context edges; no cast-node creation.
11. Build only under `/Game/_MCP_Temp` or `/Game/_MCP_Sample`.
12. Compile and dependency-audit the target.
13. Read back RigVM topology and hierarchy transform effects.
14. Prove direct solve behavior: setting a parent item with propagation changes
    the expected child global transform while preserving no-source-asset
    mutation.

Exit gate for implementation:

- `build_controlrig_recipe` reports success, compile success, dependency audit
  pass, planned/performed write evidence, and no partial mutation.
- readback confirms the `FRigUnit_SetTransform` node, pins, defaults, and link.
- direct solve proof shows the expected hierarchy transform delta.
- cleanup removes any saved temp assets created by the proof.

## Phase 7A validation-only follow-up

The sampleless follow-up adds `validate_controlrig_solver_intents` as an
UnrealMCP-native validation route and records `FRigUnit_TwoBoneIKSimplePerItem`
only as intent metadata behind `validation_only_no_sample`. This remains
evidence-only: it does not call the ControlRig authoring module, add a C++
solver allowlist entry, recipe schema, RigVM unit writer, compile, save, direct
solve proof, or asset mutation path. The implementation gate above still
controls actual solver unit expansion.
